          ":question/id": "52150036-21b2-593f-96c3-821ddd81a9cf",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-13543",
          ":question/problem": "Find $M+O-(N+M)$, if\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$M=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$N=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$O=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 6 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>",
          ":question/worked-solution": "First, we simplify the expression by distributing the subtraction over the matrices in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M+O-(N+M) & =M+O-N-M \\\\  & =\\cancel{M}+O-N-\\cancel{M} \\\\  & =O-N\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are left with a single subtraction. So, we subtract the corresponding entries of the two matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}O-N & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 6 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8-1 & 6-4 \\\\ 5-2 & 3-(-1)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
