          ":question/id": "2ce69f40-2704-5d26-9959-08c4817035a7",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-279581",
          ":question/problem": "Find $A+B-(C+B)$, if\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$C=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$A+B-(C+B)=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>{{field-4}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>",
          ":question/worked-solution": "First, we simplify the expression by distributing the subtraction over the matrices in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B-(C+B) & =A+B-C-B \\\\  & =A+\\cancel{B}-C-\\cancel{B} \\\\  & =A-C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are left with a single subtraction. So, we subtract the corresponding entries of the two matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-C & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2-8 & -5-(-2) \\\\ 7-(-4) & 0-1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -3 \\\\ 11 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
