        ":activity/steps": [
          {
            ":db/id": 17592186101859,
            ":step/content": {
              ":db/id": 17592186101954,
              ":tutorial/content": "If we want to add (or subtract) three or more matrices, all operations should be done elementwise. For example, suppose\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen we can calculate ${A}+{B}-{C}$ by performing the operations on each corresponding entry, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B-C & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1+(-1)-0 \\\\ 1+2-5 \\\\ -1+0-(-2)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
              ":tutorial/id": "f6d0bdee-d80b-596a-bef2-41b2d6429eeb",
              ":tutorial/math-academy-id": 2973,
              ":tutorial/title": "Introduction"
            },
            ":step/id": "843ddc26-4ece-5c0c-b76f-eb3b2ae356b8",
            ":step/math-academy-id": 464512,
            ":step/next": {
              ":db/id": 17592186101860
            }
          },
          {
            ":db/id": 17592186101860,
            ":step/content": {
              ":db/id": 17592186100991,
              ":knowledge-point/canonical-example": {
                ":db/id": 17592186100686,
                ":question/id": "0928c2fa-a772-5d39-a638-1b1d0e71be2f",
                ":question/math-academy-id": "e-4378",
                ":question/problem": "Calculate $A-(B-C),$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
                ":question/worked-solution": "Performing the operations on each corresponding entry, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(B-C) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}-(\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-1-0 & -1-(-5) \\\\ 2-1 & 0-1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1-(-1) & 0-4 \\\\ 2-1 & -2-(-1)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
              },
              ":knowledge-point/id": "667ac53c-36b8-56a0-9699-fe27c8373c6b",
              ":knowledge-point/key-prerequisites": [
                {
                  ":db/id": 17592186049304
                }
              ],
              ":knowledge-point/title": "Calculating the Sum or Difference of Three or More Matrices"
            },
            ":step/id": "407278d3-c813-5ac8-8cf6-2aa214dd6409",
            ":step/math-academy-id": 464513,
            ":step/next": {
              ":db/id": 17592186101861
            }
          },
          {
            ":db/id": 17592186101861,
            ":step/content": {
              ":db/id": 17592186101955,
              ":tutorial/content": "Since addition and subtraction of matrices are performed elementwise, they have the same properties as addition and subtraction of real numbers.\n\nFor example, if $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ are three $m \\times n$ matrices then we can add them in any order:\n\n$$\n(A+B)+C = A+(B+C) = A+B+C\n$$\n\nMoreover, we can distribute a subtraction over matrices in parentheses:\n\n$$\nA - (B + C) = A - B - C\n$$",
              ":tutorial/id": "fe03e3b3-f2de-50f5-b0cc-b62f7b295f8d",
              ":tutorial/math-academy-id": 2974,
              ":tutorial/title": "Properties of Matrix Addition and Subtraction"
            },
            ":step/id": "683ace4f-5219-5026-a420-485f13383a10",
            ":step/math-academy-id": 464516,
            ":step/next": {
              ":db/id": 17592186101862
            }
          },
          {
            ":db/id": 17592186101862,
            ":step/content": {
              ":db/id": 17592186100992,
              ":knowledge-point/canonical-example": {
                ":db/id": 17592186100687,
                ":question/id": "1b15db42-aba2-575c-a01e-b715450329fd",
                ":question/math-academy-id": "e-4379",
                ":question/problem": "Find $A+C-(B+A)$, if\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>",
                ":question/worked-solution": "First, we simplify the expression by distributing the subtraction over the matrices in the parentheses: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+C-(B+A) & =A+C-B-A \\\\  & =\\cancel{A}+C-B-\\cancel{A} \\\\  & =C-B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are left with a single subtraction. So, we subtract the corresponding entries of the two matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C-B & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3-3 & -1-(-1) \\\\ 1-2 & 2-0 \\\\ -6-(-4) & 1-1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
              },
              ":knowledge-point/id": "16e62b0e-adda-5d35-aeb9-961057dce8f0",
