              ":question/id": "7b0757c3-add5-56d5-bdb9-9aa972bc2c60",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-809",
              ":question/problem": "Simplify the expression $-(2x-1.3)$.",
              ":question/worked-solution": "First, we rewrite the negative sign as multiplication by $(-1)\\mathbin$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -(2x-1.3) \\\\ &= (-1)(2x-1.3) \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we distribute the $(-1)$ to each term in the parentheses, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} (-1)(2x-1.3) \\\\ &= (-1) (2x)-(-1) (1.3) \\\\ &= -2x-(-1.3) \\\\ &= -2x+1.3 \\end{aligned}\n$$"
            },
            ":knowledge-point/id": "5704b343-dbff-5420-8c13-f30e316d6b8d",
            ":knowledge-point/title": "Distributing the Negative Sign over the Difference of Two Terms"
          },
          {
